# Agent-tool state, written by the tools themselves. Same rule as everything above: a
# formatter and a generator cannot both own a file. These are not merely generated once
# — they are rewritten during a session, so formatting them buys a clean check that goes
# red again on its own. `.headroom_wrap_marker.json` holds a live pid and port and is
# rewritten every run; `settings.local.json` is machine-local by convention; `.serena/`
# is serena's generated project state.
#
# Deliberately not the whole of `.claude/`: `settings.json`, `agents/`, `hooks/` and
# `skills/` are hand-written project automation and stay formatted.
.claude/.headroom_wrap_*
.claude/settings.local.json
.serena/
